N:HOW READ (2026-11-11): the clip's sustained part (harmonic/percussive separation, which takes out the drum strokes and the jingles) was pitch-tracked between G3 and E6; the singing sits about 40 cents above A=440 at the start and sags 20-30 cents by the long F, which is taken as the tonic (7.9-9.4 s, with the octave below). Phrases: the lead 0.2-4.7 s (B to C6, then B, A, G, A, B flat, A, a dip to C5, A held), the seconds 5.6-9.4 s (F sharp, B, E flat, E, F held), the next phrase 9.5-13.4 s (a quick turn G, F sharp, B, F sharp, then E, B4, G, D, G, A, F, A, B flat 4, A flat 4), drum only 13.5-15.7 s, and the start of the next (F sharp, 15.8 s). One eighth here is one drum stroke (about 0.30 s). Scored against the pitch track, each phrase aligned at its own start: 53% of voiced frames in all (lead 53%, seconds 64%, the third phrase 34%), lower than a steady instrument would give because of the slides.
N:UNCERTAIN: almost everything: the B naturals (between B flat and B, perhaps slides from C); the F sharps (perhaps F sung sharp, a semitone above the tonic); E flat or D at 6.5-6.8 s (it sits 250 cents below F); the quick turn at 9.6-10.0 s; every length; which voice is the lead and which the seconds.
